  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 917 PM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nUpper troughing that was holding strong over the eastern third of\nthe CONUS should begin moving off the East Coast, as upper ridging \nslowly builds in from the west. This will help bring a gradual \nwarming trend far as temperatures for the new week. Expect another\nchilly Sun night with lows from the upper 20s to mid 30s, and \nhighs Mon in the mid/upper 50s. A slow warming trend can be \nexpected as we go further into next week. Lows will range in the\n30s, with highs in the lower 60s Tue, and in the mid/upper 60s on\nWed/Thu respectively. At this time, dry conditions should prevail\ninto next Thu.",
